.TH SNMPDIGGER 1 "2026-09-04" "snmpdigger" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
snmpdigger \- fancy TUI SNMP browser, live grapher and network discovery tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snmpdigger
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger discover
.I cidr
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger walk
.I host
.RI [ oid ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger get
.I host
.I oid
.RI [ oid ... ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger identify
.I host
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B snmpdigger config path
.br
.B snmpdigger version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snmpdigger
is a terminal application for exploring SNMP agents.
.PP
Run with no arguments it starts in full\-screen TUI mode and opens a connection
dialog asking for the target host, port, SNMP version and the matching
credentials (community string for v1/v2c, or user / security level / auth and
privacy parameters for v3).  Once connected it walks the MIB/OID tree and lets
you browse it in a searchable, filterable, sortable list showing the numeric
OID, the resolved human\-readable name, the type and the live value.  Values are
polled continuously on an adjustable interval.
.PP
A graph tab plots any counter or gauge as a live line chart, bar chart, gauge,
sparkline, large number or heatmap.  A discovery tab (and the
.B discover
sub\-command) sweeps an IPv4 CIDR range for SNMP\-speaking hosts and identifies
them from their system group.  A settings tab persists everything to
.IR ~/.config/snmpdigger/config.yaml .
.PP
The sub\-commands provide non\-interactive access to the same engine for scripting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-community " string"
Community string for SNMP v1/v2c (default:
.IR public ).
.TP
.BI \-\-version " v1|v2c|v3"
SNMP protocol version (default:
.IR v2c ).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
UDP port of the agent (default:
.IR 161 ).
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start against a built\-in synthetic agent; no network access.  TUI only.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " name"
SNMPv3 security name.
.TP
.BI \-\-level " noAuthNoPriv|authNoPriv|authPriv"
SNMPv3 security level.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth\-proto " MD5|SHA|SHA224|SHA256|SHA384|SHA512"
SNMPv3 authentication protocol.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth\-pass " string"
SNMPv3 authentication passphrase.
.TP
.BI \-\-priv\-proto " DES|AES|AES192|AES256"
SNMPv3 privacy protocol.
.TP
.BI \-\-priv\-pass " string"
SNMPv3 privacy passphrase.
.TP
.BI \-\-context " string"
SNMPv3 context name.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/snmpdigger/config.yaml
Persisted settings and the most recently used connection profile.  Honours
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the TUI and connect interactively:
.B snmpdigger
.TP
Explore the interface without a device:
.B snmpdigger --demo
.TP
Discover every SNMP host on a subnet:
.B snmpdigger discover 192.168.1.0/24 --community public
.TP
Walk a subtree from the shell:
.B snmpdigger walk 10.0.0.1 1.3.6.1.2.1.2 --version v2c --community public
.TP
Identify a device:
.B snmpdigger identify 10.0.0.1
